## SYNTHESIS OF COMPOUNDS
ZIF-20: $Z\mathrm{n}(\mathrm{Pur})_{2}$ · $(\mathrm{DMF})_{0.75}(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O})_{1.5}$ . A solid mixture of zinc nitrate tetrahydrate $\mathrm{Zn(NO_{3})_{2}{\cdot}4H_{2}O}$ (65 mg, 0. 25 mmol, EM Science) and purine ( $150\mathrm{mg}$ , $1.25\mathrm{mmol}$ , Fluka or Sigma) was dissolved in $5\mathrm{ml}$ DMF (Fisher) in a $20\mathrm{ml}$ vial to obtain a slightly turbid solution. The vial was tightly capped and heated at $65^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ in an isothermal oven for 3 days to yield pale yellow octahedral crystals along with a small amount of powder. After unassisted cooling of the vial to room temperature, the powder product was removed by decanting with mother liquor and washed three times with DMF $(5\mathrm{ml})$ ). The crystals were dried in air for $30\mathrm{min}$ (yield: $48~\mathrm{mg}$ , $50\%$ based on $\mathrm{Zn}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}4\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\rangle$ ). Elemental analysis: Calculated for $\begin{array}{r}{{\mathrm{Zn}}({\mathrm{Pur}})_{2}{\cdot}({\mathrm{DMF}})_{0.75}({\mathrm{H}}_{2}{\mathrm{O}})_{1.5}{\colon}{\mathrm{C}},38.17{\mathrm{;H}},}\end{array}$ 3.73; N, 31.80. Found: C, 37.93; H, 3.52; N, $31.85\%$ . Fourier-transform infrared (KBr, $4,000{-}400\mathrm{cm}^{-1}$ ): 3,433(br), 3,098(w), 3,065(w), 3,036(w), 2,930(w), 2,856(w), 1,670(s), 1,589(s), 1,568(m), 1,477(s), 1,398(s), 1,310(s), 1,221(s), 1,192(m), 1,094(m), 1,020(w), 924(m), 804 $(\mathrm{m})$ , 791 $(\mathbf{m})$ , 683(w), 644(m), 621(w), 575(w), 498(w), 403(w).
