## MEASUREMENTS
Powder X-ray diffraction data were collected using a Bruker D8-Discover $\theta-2\theta$ diffractometer in reflectance Bragg–Brentano geometry at $40\mathrm{kV,40\mathrm{mA}}$ $(1,600\mathrm{W})$ for Cu $\mathrm{K}\alpha$ radiation $\mathit{\Omega}\lambda=1.5406\mathrm{\AA}$ ). TGA was carried out using a TA Q500 thermal analysis system. Fourier-transform infrared spectra of samples prepared as KBr pellets were measured using a Nicolet FT-IR Impact 400 system.
